WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.467
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.901
How great does that look when
you come out and see all the --

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:07.067
-Hot.
-Yeah, hot is exactly right.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:09.100
Exactly right.
We got a lot to talk about.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.534
Since I last saw you, you got
engaged to the lovely Megan Fox.

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:13.901
Congratulations.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:16.367
Congratulations.
-It's great.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:22.467
-Also, your latest album,
"Mainstream Sellout," came out

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.767
in March and went right
to number one.

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
Not too shabby, bud.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:29.801
-Thank you.
-Number one, not too shabby.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.901
And on June 8th, you're going to
kick off a global tour.

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:36.501
Global. This is your first
big arena tour.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:39.567
Venues sold out in a day,
by the way.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:41.033
Dude, you couldn't be hotter
right now.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:44.634
-You're stroking my ego.
-Sorry about that. I apologize.

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:47.901
What are the shows gonna be like
when you do the arena tours?

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:53.133
-You know how, like, shows have
big LED screens

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.801
and all that stuff?
-Yeah, of course, yeah.

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.067
-Yeah, we scratched all that.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:58.334
We're like, "A good showman
just needs a show."

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:01.100
-But you've played kind of
every venue out there.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.367
-Dude, I can tell you Wi-Fi
codes to like bars

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:06.767
in Blackfoot, Idaho.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:07.934
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.334
Yeah, you have
those Wi-Fi codes.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:11.400
-I can tell you the door code to
some of these venues.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.734
-So you've seen it all.
-Yeah, all of them.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:15.534
Except the arenas,
so I'm excited.

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.200
-Yeah. I was gonna say.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.934
You know what? There's a quote
that I'm sure you heard this.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:21.501
But I just have to tell you that

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:24.200
Mick Jagger said something about
you recently.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.601
Can I read it to you?
-Please.

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:27.901
-"In rock music --"

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:30.100
[ as Mick Jagger ] In rock
music, you need energy.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.067
[ Normal voice ] Yeah, sorry.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.334
"You need energy,

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:37.167
and there have not been a lot of
new rock singers around.

00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.400
Now, there are a few.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.968
You have Yungblud
and Machine Gun Kelly.

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.934
That kind of post-punk vibe
makes me think

00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:45.934
there still is a bit of life
to rock 'n' roll."

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:49.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:51.133
Mick Jagger!
-Alright!

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.834
-Mick Jagger!

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:56.000
-Yeah.
-How does that feel?

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.367
Did you -- When did you hear
that he said that?

00:01:58.367 --> 00:01:59.868
-On a bad day.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:02.300
-That's a good day to hear it.
-Absolutely.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.701
It was like -- It was a day --

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:08.067
I'm polarizing to people
for some reason,

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:11.834
so there was a lot of -- Like,
you can just feel a lot of hate

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:14.701
coming at you sometimes,
and I just remember, like,

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.467
I was feeling it that morning,
and then I read that quote

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:19.801
and then I just said...

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:20.901
"I didn't say it."

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.567
-"I didn't say it.
Yeah, he said it, not me."

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:26.400
That's got to make you feel
fantastic.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.467
-Yeah, it was great.
-Have you ever met Mick Jagger?

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.033
-No, but it would be hard for me

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.234
to be across from him
and not do this.

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:33.567
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:34.901
And just do it.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.968
'Cause you want to start doing
the rooster with him?

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.634
-I might.
-Yeah.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:41.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:42.601
You have to kind of do it
when you see him.

00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:44.067
♪♪

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.534
Yeah, that's the way -- Yeah,
that's what I'm talking about!

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:50.000
You got to do that.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.834
Congrats on "Good Mourning."

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:54.300
It's in select theaters
and on demand now.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.567
Mourning, by the way,
is spelled M-O-U-R.

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.067
-Yes.
-Yeah, "Good Mourning."

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:01.067
It's a comedy that you wrote
based on a text

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:03.267
that you got from a girlfriend?

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:04.601
-From Megan.
-From Megan?

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:05.968
-Yes.
-Oh.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:08.567
-I'm a one-woman man.
-Of course you are, yeah.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:13.501
So, you got a text from Megan
and so it just -- What happened?

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:17.334
You spiraled out?
-Yeah, it's like -- it started

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:19.267
with, like, Megan's
very just in nature.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:22.300
She's like -- That's where
her head's always at.

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.033
The text -- It was this long
paragraph that started with

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:28.667
like, "A raven came and sat next
to me in a tree."

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:31.434
And then, you know,
it was all this stuff.

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:33.434
And then she got on a plane
and went to Europe

00:03:33.434 --> 00:03:36.100
and didn't take her phone and I
was just like, "What is that?"

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.634
Like, "You can't leave me
with this."

00:03:38.634 --> 00:03:39.968
And it was right when I was --

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:43.167
when we were starting to,
like, be serious.

00:03:43.167 --> 00:03:45.234
I just like took the message
to all my friends

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:47.300
who aren't in relationships
for relationship advice,

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.834
which is, like, great,
and they were like,

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:52.133
"That's not good, dude."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:56.801
And now, after doing all this
press for the movie, I'm like,

00:03:56.801 --> 00:04:00.067
"Why did I write --" Like,
instead of just waiting

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:02.701
to talk about it, I like, got
manic and wrote a whole movie

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:06.868
and got all this cast involved
and spent the studio's money.

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:08.367
And I'm just like,
"I should have just

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.400
waited a week and talked."
-Yeah, and talked to her, yeah.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.467
But you turned out
with a great product.

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:15.434
When you do these movies,
it's a big deal.

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:18.767
You also play it in front of
audiences, like test audiences.

00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:21.534
And you were telling me there's
a couple things that got cut

00:04:21.534 --> 00:04:25.334
from this movie
that were high-budget things.

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.534
Big-budget stuff.
I mean, like -- Yeah.

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:29.300
What were they, like, CGI?

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.934
-No, no. We were like,
"Let's just go real."

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:36.200
So, we had a $50,000 lobster --

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:37.801
[ Laughs ]

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:43.300
We spent $50,000 between this
lobster and an electric eel.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.400
-You spent $50,000
on this lobster puppet?

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:51.267
-Is there a picture of the eel?

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:54.734
But it might have gone to
the LED lights that are put in.

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:57.734
None of which, either of these
make an appearance in the movie.

00:04:57.734 --> 00:05:00.133
They all got cut because we,
like, screened it

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.267
and they had like
a 15-minute section

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:03.734
'cause we thought
it was so funny.

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:07.100
We were like, "Oh, this lobster
section is going to crush."

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.200
And it did the opposite.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.934
Everyone left with -- The only
note pretty much for the whole

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:15.567
screening was like,
"Great, laughed my ass off.

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:19.634
Why was there this lobster scene
that was 15 minutes?

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:21.601
Like, what -- I hated it."

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:23.767
-Where is the puppet now?
-We don't know.

00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:25.667
[ Laughter ]
You know what?

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:29.200
We probably need our money back.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.734
I feel like I've seen five of
these backstage in your show.

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:33.000
-Yeah, we make them.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.033
We don't have $50,000
lobster puppets.

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:37.100
-It was for puppeteer costs too.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.167
-Wowzers!

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.701
-We were super meticulous like,
"We need its claws to move.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:44.767
We need its mouth to move."
We gave it abs.

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:46.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:50.234
-Abs. I mean -- Well, it's
getting its play tonight.

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:52.601
-There we go.
That's almost kind of worth it.

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:55.367
-Your character is trying to get
an audition

00:05:55.367 --> 00:05:57.701
for the role of Batman
in this movie.

00:05:57.701 --> 00:05:59.334
-Yeah.
-Did you know that "The Batman"

00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:02.067
was coming out
when you were writing this?

00:06:02.067 --> 00:06:05.434
-No. It was just,
like, very serendipitous.

00:06:05.434 --> 00:06:07.234
It just worked out like that.

00:06:07.234 --> 00:06:11.934
It's a crazy story, because
Batman -- Batman and the entity

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:16.267
just kept popping up because,
you know, "Batman" came out

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:18.000
a month before
this movie came out.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.200
And we were like, "Oh, my God,
that's great. This is crazy."

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.601
And then also a month ago I was
having my birthday party,

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:25.567
and you know, there was this one
Easter where I was like,

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:27.300
"Hey, Pete, you got to come.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.133
You know, let's go to
my friend's house for Easter."

00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:31.067
He pulled up and he had 40s
and he was like,

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:32.300
"Let's do this thing."

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:33.634
And we went and it was
Sandra Bullock's house.

00:06:33.634 --> 00:06:36.734
We walked in. It was Jen Aniston
and all these, like --

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:38.901
And Pete was like,
"Why would you do this to me?

00:06:38.901 --> 00:06:40.100
We look so stupid.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:41.901
We have 40 ounces
and we're at Sandra Bullock's.

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.267
Why didn't you tell me this is
where we were going?"

00:06:43.267 --> 00:06:45.934
-America's sweetheart.

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:48.567
-So, it's like my birthday
last month. And he texts me.

00:06:48.567 --> 00:06:50.067
He's like, "Hey, I'm about to
come to your party.

00:06:50.067 --> 00:06:51.934
Can I bring a plus-one?"
I was like, "Yeah, of course."

00:06:51.934 --> 00:06:54.834
And he pulls up and his plus-one
is Robert Pattinson.

00:06:54.834 --> 00:06:56.434
And I was like,
"You brought Batman?"

00:06:56.434 --> 00:06:57.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.701 --> 00:07:00.634
-Surprise!
-Yeah, it's so funny.

00:07:00.634 --> 00:07:02.000
Everyone just kept coming up

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.767
like, "Dude, is Batman
at your birthday party?

00:07:03.767 --> 00:07:05.701
It's funny when you become
Batman because no one

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:07.767
refers to you anymore as your
actual name. You're just Batman.

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:09.334
-Yeah, for the rest of
your life, you're Batman.

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:10.267
-You're Batman.
-Yeah.

00:07:10.267 --> 00:07:11.767
Did you know Robert before?

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:15.834
-Yeah, again, always just out,
seeing him and stuff like that.

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:18.567
But this was a -- it's just --
But now he's Batman.

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:20.067
So I'm just like,
"What up, dude?

00:07:20.067 --> 00:07:22.334
I know we know each other,
but you're kind of Batman now."

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:24.000
-Now you're Batman, yeah.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.000
Can we set up the film
for anyone that wants to

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.601
know more about the film?
-No.

00:07:28.601 --> 00:07:31.834
I'm just kidding.
No one go see it.

00:07:31.834 --> 00:07:34.467
-It's a comedy. It's a comedy.
-It's a comedy, yes.

00:07:34.467 --> 00:07:38.167
It kind of just goes back to the
classic days of, like, gag humor

00:07:38.167 --> 00:07:41.934
and like, just, you know,
$50,000 lobster puppets

00:07:41.934 --> 00:07:45.100
that we thought
were going to crush.

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.067
The cast is oddly great.

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:50.467
The budget was this big
and the cast is this big.

00:07:50.467 --> 00:07:53.300
-Snoop Dogg is the voice
of a talking joint.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.367
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:55.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:55.667 --> 00:07:58.100
Not too shabby. I mean, you kind
of hit a home run there.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.200
[ Applause ]
Hit a home run right there.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.200
That's all you need. That's all
you need to really say.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.367
I want to show a clip.

00:08:03.367 --> 00:08:05.100
Here's Colson Baker
in "Good Mourning."

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:07.367
Take a look at this.

00:08:07.367 --> 00:08:09.501
-Leo?

00:08:09.501 --> 00:08:12.467
What the [bleep]
did you just do?

00:08:12.467 --> 00:08:16.167
-London, what is this dust?

00:08:16.167 --> 00:08:20.400
-That's not dust.
That's people, man.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.601
-Homey, did you just bring
the dead grandma vase?

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:24.434
-Oh!

00:08:24.434 --> 00:08:25.968
-We can fix this.

00:08:25.968 --> 00:08:28.067
I think that was actually the
cousin that no one really liked.

00:08:28.067 --> 00:08:31.300
So...we got to pick him up.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:35.067
-Whoa, I ain't [bleep]
human remains, man.

00:08:35.067 --> 00:08:37.467
-Dude, Leo.

00:08:37.467 --> 00:08:40.834
You did it.

00:08:40.834 --> 00:08:43.400
-It's all good. It's all good.

00:08:47.534 --> 00:08:49.767
At least it was
just one of 'em.

00:08:49.767 --> 00:08:51.968
I mean, it doesn't even look
that bad, guys.

00:08:54.167 --> 00:08:56.734
[ Applause ]

00:08:56.734 --> 00:08:59.434
-That's exactly right.

00:08:59.434 --> 00:09:03.534
Colson Baker, a.k.a.
Machine Gun Kelly, everybody.

00:09:03.534 --> 00:09:07.734
"Good Mourning" is in select
theaters and on demand now.

00:09:07.734 --> 00:09:09.801
Catch him on tour this summer.

